No, it's a friendship.

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:19.320
Oh, friendship, yeah.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:24.060
It's friendship and with over 35 years

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:27.480
of that continuing to
happen, like constantly.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:29.394
Friendship is still happening.

00:01:29.394 --> 00:01:31.040
You know, it's--

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:33.790
Despite the doubts in the
comments from time to time.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:34.623
Right.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:36.910
And I would say

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:41.187
to be friends as long as we have

00:01:41.187 --> 00:01:46.187
and to not get like
concerned comments from fans

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:49.550
who are only seeing us
through the lens of the lens--

00:01:49.550 --> 00:01:50.383
Lens of the lens.

00:01:50.383 --> 00:01:52.370
Would be, that would be weird.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:55.780
I mean for us not to be
comfortable enough with each other

00:01:55.780 --> 00:02:00.660
that sometimes, these honest
moments of tension come through

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.290
in the things we createm I
think that's a beautiful thing

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:05.703
because it's, again, it's those,

00:02:06.587 --> 00:02:09.590
everything in friendship is not rosy.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:13.010
Friendship, in general, is very difficult

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:16.737
and as I've look through these questions

00:02:16.737 --> 00:02:21.540
that we're gonna discuss
from mythical beasts,

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.813
it's a good reminder of,

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:29.300
to me, about how much work it takes.

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.000
I don't wanna show our hand here

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.630
but it does take a lot of work

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:38.170
and there's no clear answers
because on any given day

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:41.560
in any given friendship,
there could be any scenario

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:43.120
that you've never experienced before

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:45.150
and you may not know anyone
who's been through it

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:48.420
so you kinda, like, what do I do?

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:49.940
So we'll talk about some of that.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:52.410
Yeah, and like all relationships,

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:57.120
they have their projects that
have to receive attention

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.490
and so, hopefully, we
can offer some insights

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.060
but speaking of our friendship--

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:02.560
And viewing friendship as,

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:04.810
of your friend as a project,

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:06.693
it's maybe a bad place to start.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:09.700
Well, you know what I mean.

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:11.900
It requires ongoing attention

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.370
but a person is not a project,
that's not what I meant.

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:18.170
But speaking of friendship
and maintaining friendships,

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:22.600
I mean we did something that
is just about as friendly

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:23.940
as you could possibly do.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:27.650
We went and went on
paddleboats this past weekend.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:30.860
Yeah, me and Rhett went out
on a paddleboat together.

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:32.560
Can you picture this two of us on,

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:37.660
at Echo Park, there's a lake which I guess

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:39.590
is called Echo Lake, is it?

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:40.950
I just call it Echo Park Lake.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:41.864
I don't know if that's what it is.

00:03:41.864 --> 00:03:43.080
Echo Park.

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:43.913
But--

00:03:43.913 --> 00:03:44.746
Echo Park Lake.

00:03:44.746 --> 00:03:45.579
It's like the most,

00:03:45.579 --> 00:03:49.500
one of the most LA things
that you can do is get on--

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:50.333
Echo Lake?

00:03:50.333 --> 00:03:51.166
Echo Park Lake.

00:03:51.166 --> 00:03:51.999
Oh.
Echo Park Lake.

00:03:51.999 --> 00:03:52.832
Echo Park Lake.
Is get on one

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:54.420
of these giant swans

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:57.278
that is a paddleboat that
can hold like five people

00:03:57.278 --> 00:04:01.750
and paddle around this pond
and I've been by this place

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:03.110
so many times, and I've been like--

00:04:03.110 --> 00:04:03.943
Me too.

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.520
Gotta get out on one of those paddleboats.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:08.623
You'll see it in like,

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:14.360
if a commercial decides
to shoot in Los Angeles,

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:17.064
especially if they need
like a picturesque scene,

00:04:17.064 --> 00:04:20.823
like if it's an ad for a medication,

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:23.550
they'll shoot at Echo Park.

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:26.240
Now, they'll film at such an angle

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:31.130
where like you can from
one side of the lake,

00:04:31.130 --> 00:04:32.960
shoot across these fountains,

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.120
there's three fountains
that are grouped together

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:38.050
that shoot water, probably
50 feet in the air.

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:39.070
Straight up in the air.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:42.140
And then you shoot past that
and you can see the skyline

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:43.420
of Downtown Los Angeles.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:44.253
It's very beautiful.

00:04:44.253 --> 00:04:46.350
But you just got to make sure that you,

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:49.050
that you film the proper angle

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:51.130
around the homeless encampments.

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:52.010
There are a few of those.

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:52.843
Right, yeah.

00:04:52.843 --> 00:04:53.830
But they're very well--

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:54.860
They probably get them to leave

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.380
when they're about a shoot of commercial.

00:04:56.380 --> 00:05:00.170
They're very well-maintained
homeless camps

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:03.170
because, I mean they're like,
there's a camp under this tree

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:05.070
and then you go to the
next stream there's a camp

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:09.820
but, I mean, they got nice
tents and there's this one guy,

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:12.570
he had a frigging, where we parked,

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:14.307
he had a flat screen
television beside his tent

00:05:14.307 --> 00:05:17.210
and I was like, "How on earth?"

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:18.990
And then before I could get my answer,

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:20.260
I was like, "Oh, solar panels."

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:21.520
Yeah, a solar-powered--

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.010
Dude had solar panels--

00:05:23.010 --> 00:05:24.187
Flat screen TV out there.

00:05:24.187 --> 00:05:25.793
And a nice tent.

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:29.680
And so, it was like this
is prime real estate.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.400
I made a note.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:32.233
Right.

00:05:32.233 --> 00:05:35.300
If I need to live out of a tent,

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:36.133
LA is a great place to be.

00:05:36.133 --> 00:05:37.360
First of all, you've
got to get a flat screen

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:38.720
and a solar panel.
You gotta move to LA.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:39.553
I'm already here.

00:05:39.553 --> 00:05:40.930
And there's just so much going on.

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:45.460
I mean the thing about any
outdoor space in Los Angeles

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:48.410
on the weekend, really, anytime
but especially the weekend,

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:51.930
is there's just so much happening.

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:55.670
There's so many people there
and I know for a lot of people,

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:57.727
that can be a problem because you're like,

00:05:57.727 --> 00:05:59.700
"Why can't I just go to an open space?"

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:01.240
Now, you can easily get to open spaces

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:03.630
where you won't see a soul, you
decide to go outside of town

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:07.110
but it was just like so many
people of all walks of life

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:10.810
almost as if the people
had been manufactured

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:12.700
for the sake of a movie.

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:13.930
Or for an insurance commercial.

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:14.880
Walking around--
I mean

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:15.713
medication commercial.

00:06:15.713 --> 00:06:17.100
I mean you got people selling things.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:22.100
You got this guy giving
free vegan ice cream samples

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:24.670
next to a guy selling--

00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:25.503
Ceviche.

00:06:25.503 --> 00:06:27.400
Chevice and then you got the taco place

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:28.690
and it's just, I don't
even know if these people

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:30.980
have licenses or permits.

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:33.240
I don't even care and then--

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:36.130
So picture me and Rhett holding hands

00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:40.701
and skipping around this
lake together hopping on--

00:06:40.701 --> 00:06:41.534
That exactly

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:42.880
how it happened.
Hopping on a swan

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:47.230
and just peddling out there
with our jean cutoff shorts.

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:48.100
Yeah, if you--

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:49.120
And our thighs--

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:50.013
I'm sorry to disappoint you--

00:06:50.013 --> 00:06:50.846
Tanned.

00:06:50.846 --> 00:06:53.209
But we actually didn't
get on the same swan.

00:06:53.209 --> 00:06:58.209
My sister-in-law and two
nieces were in town and then,

00:06:58.914 --> 00:07:01.797
I think your wife had the idea to be like,

00:07:01.797 --> 00:07:05.297
"Hey, let's all go to the swans,

00:07:05.297 --> 00:07:06.377
"let's all get on the paddleboats.

00:07:06.377 --> 00:07:08.177
"Let's do this thing that
we've talked about doing

00:07:08.177 --> 00:07:10.170
"for 10 years and we've never done."

00:07:10.170 --> 00:07:15.090
So it was you and your
wife and two of your kids.

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:15.923
No.

00:07:15.923 --> 00:07:16.756
One of your kids.

00:07:16.756 --> 00:07:19.780
No, me and Christy were on a pedal boat,

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:20.640
and they call 'em pedal--

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:21.763
No, I'm just saying--
Not paddleboat,

00:07:21.763 --> 00:07:22.596
by the way.
I'm just saying

00:07:22.596 --> 00:07:24.044
who was there at this event.

00:07:24.044 --> 00:07:25.816
And then my wife--

00:07:25.816 --> 00:07:26.970
But we can do it by boat.
And my son.

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:28.920
So, me and Christy were on a boat.

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:29.960
And just you and Christy.

00:07:29.960 --> 00:07:30.793
Just me and Christy.

00:07:30.793 --> 00:07:32.010
I don't how you worked that out.

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:34.490
Because you volunteered
to take the youngest kid--

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:38.250
The kids, so Shepherd and
his first cousin Adeline,

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:41.260
my brother's daughter, is like,

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.876
they are each other's favorite people.

00:07:43.876 --> 00:07:44.990
They're the same age.

00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:46.920
Same age within like a couple months

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:49.230
and they just love each other,

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:51.310
they love spending time with each other,

00:07:51.310 --> 00:07:54.293
they're into all the same
things and they just,

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:57.730
two peas in a pod as you say in the South.

00:07:57.730 --> 00:08:01.140
And they really love to include
Lando, which is very cool.

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:03.510
He and Shepherd are really tight

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:05.170
but Lando's a little bit younger

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:07.450
so I think it's nice when Adeline

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:09.410
enters the equation that
they still wanna include him

00:08:09.410 --> 00:08:11.480
and invite him over to
swim and stuff like that.

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:16.050
And by the way, you do know that Shepherd

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:20.800
jumps off of the roof
of the shed that covers

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:23.010
the back half of your patio.
Behind.

00:08:23.010 --> 00:08:24.400
Into the pool.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.150
Yeah, they recently
discovered they could do that.

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:28.430
Well, they invited Lando
over and then Lando comes,

00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:30.530
we pick him up and he's coming back home

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:32.130
and you know how Lando is.

00:08:32.130 --> 00:08:34.700
He like had this sheepish look on his face

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:37.533
and I remembered I was like,

00:08:39.087 --> 00:08:42.100
"Lando, did you jump off
of the roof into the pool?"

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:45.530
He was like, "Yeah, Shepherd
told me I should do it."

00:08:45.530 --> 00:08:46.560
Oh, Lando did it.

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:47.393
And he did it.

00:08:47.393 --> 00:08:48.226
That's awesome.

00:08:48.226 --> 00:08:49.710
And then he started crying.

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:51.463
He was like don't be mad at me.

00:08:52.403 --> 00:08:53.850
I was like, "We're not mad at you."

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:56.230
Boy, Shepard has never
cried about anything

00:08:56.230 --> 00:08:57.520
except not getting his way.

00:08:57.520 --> 00:09:00.410
Definitely never cried about
getting caught for something.

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:03.650
So the three of them wanted
to be in the same boat

00:09:03.650 --> 00:09:05.530
and then you stepped up to the plate.

00:09:05.530 --> 00:09:07.310
Well, I knew an adult had,

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:09.980
I like being the fun uncle, you know.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:10.857
The funcle.

00:09:10.857 --> 00:09:14.130
And I'm quite a funcle and I was like

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:16.010
I'm gonna go out with
these kids, it'll be fun.

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:17.260
We can drive through,

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:20.320
I knew they would want
me to drive really close.

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:22.658
Drive, I think, paddle.

00:09:22.658 --> 00:09:23.520
Do you drive a boat?

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:26.660
You do drive a boat
because there is a rudder.

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:28.880
They wanted me to go really
close to the giant fountains

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:31.070
because the wind is like blowing the water

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:32.650
that's going 50 feet in the air

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:35.350
and of course, you can go
right under it and get wet

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:37.910
and it's like going on
the log ride at Disney.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:40.700
Christy and I watched you do
that from a safe distance.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:41.533
Yeah.

00:09:41.533 --> 00:09:42.570
We spent most of our time

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:44.950
trying to get an Instagramable photo.

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:46.380
You know how that is?

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:47.213
Did you get one?

00:09:47.213 --> 00:09:50.430
Yes, you know what, she did gram one.

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:52.120
So, I think she got what she needed.

00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:55.830
I always forget that that's
a thing that you can do.

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:57.420
I think it's just a sign of my age

00:09:57.420 --> 00:10:01.270
that social media is still
just not a part of my DNA.

00:10:01.270 --> 00:10:02.232
So I'm doing things--
Oh, I think you focused

00:10:02.232 --> 00:10:04.470
on the right thing, man, that was good.

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:07.890
I know but, you mean,
this is what we do, man.

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:09.225
It's like if you're in a giant--

00:10:09.225 --> 00:10:10.058
Oh, we're talking about it.

00:10:10.058 --> 00:10:11.960
If you're in a giant swan,

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:14.290
you should get a picture of
yourself in a giant swan.

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:16.060
There's a freaking coffee shop out there.

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:17.780
I got a lavender.

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:19.680
You make it sound like it's
in the middle of the lake.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.053
It's on the dock.

00:10:21.053 --> 00:10:23.360
You have to walk through
a little coffee shop

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:26.160
that serves breakfast burritos
on the weekends, what?

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:26.993
Yeah, I love it.

00:10:26.993 --> 00:10:29.630
I got a lavender latte and
I'm not ashamed of that.

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:31.760
I love when lavender is in things.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:35.140
It's one of my favorite
flavors to be in things.

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:37.690
Something that seems like
it shouldn't be ingested.

00:10:37.690 --> 00:10:38.960
Yeah, let's eat perfume.

00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:40.950
That sounds like a good weekend.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:44.650
This lavender latte made me so happy.

00:10:44.650 --> 00:10:48.950
It's just almost as happy as
being in a swan on a lake.

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:51.360
Chasing swans, did you notice that?

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:53.970
You could chase other
swans with this giant swan.

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:55.710
Do you think that the little swans

